 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,7 +19,42 @@\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n+    Current method: log-transformed skewed input and pairwise products to capture\n+    interactions.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+\n+    # Log-transform right-skewed x3 (guard against zero/negative)\n+    log_x3 = math.log(max(x3, 1e-10))\n+\n+    # Pairwise products to capture interaction effects\n+    prod_features = [\n+        x1 * x2,\n+        x1 * x3,\n+        x1 * x4,\n+        x1 * x5,\n+        x1 * x6,\n+        x2 * x3,\n+        x2 * x4,\n+        x2 * x5,\n+        x2 * x6,\n+        x3 * x4,\n+        x3 * x5,\n+        x3 * x6,\n+        x4 * x5,\n+        x4 * x6,\n+        x5 * x6,\n+    ]\n+\n+    # Sign of pairwise products for quadrant information\n+    sign_features = [1 if p >= 0 else -1 for p in prod_features]\n+\n+    # Standard normal features\n+    norm_features = [x1, x2, x6]\n+\n+    # Log-transformed skewed feature\n+    log_features = [log_x3]\n+\n+    # Combine all features\n+    return norm_features + log_features + sign_features\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
